% Verification convention (revised 2026-09-11, replaces VERIFIED/CLASSIC inline tags):
%   the comment line(s) directly ABOVE each entry read
%     % [VERIFIED yyyy-mm-dd] <source URL or local PDF> -- what the source confirmed
%   or
%     % [UNVERIFIED] <reason>
%   Comments sit outside the entries because classic BibTeX does not treat the percent
%   sign as a comment inside an entry.  Never type the at-sign in a comment line: BibTeX
%   reads it as the start of an entry.
%   "Crossref record" = the metadata the publisher deposited for that DOI, read through
%   https://api.crossref.org/works/<DOI> on the date given.  "DBLP record" = the dblp record
%   for the DOI, read through the dblp SPARQL endpoint https://sparql.dblp.org/sparql (the
%   dblp.org web search serves a bot check to scripts).
%   A publisher page that is no longer online is cited through its Internet Archive capture,
%   with the capture timestamp.  Source code is cited from the publisher's own repository at a
%   pinned commit, read through the GitHub REST API.
%   A web page (game rules, patch notes, API terms) is cited from its publisher's own page with
%   the page's own date: for a wiki page, the revision read and its permanent link; for a Riot
%   page, the publication or last-updated date the page states (section 10, added 2026-09-14).
